WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.802 line:0%
-How are you doing
with all that?

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:04.036 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:05.838 line:0%
-My old man
would have hated this.

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.274 line:0%
What are you doing?

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:10.510
Go after the Marcy Killers
as the bad guys.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.178
Leave your fellow cops alone.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:13.545
-Elliot, that was
a different time.

00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:14.981
That was your father.

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.016
You had to go along
to get along.

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.986
-He's a tough-ass.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:23.456
Not perfect...

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:26.992
but he's a good cop.

00:00:26.992 --> 00:00:30.029
-Elliot.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:31.431
My friend.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:33.699
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:35.168
You're doing the right thing.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:36.268
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:36.268 --> 00:00:38.170
We're here with
Mariska Hargitay,

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.672
Christopher Meloni.

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:41.774
-I didn't realize that.
It came out.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:44.477
-You don't watch my show?
-Must be --

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.212
-Hey, not now, Seth,
we're talking.

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:47.914
-No, I understand.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:50.049
-[ Laughs ]
I never saw that scene.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:51.250
-You never saw that scene?

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:54.153
-I said I didn't realize
it came out so sexy.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:55.788
-Oh.
-And he said,

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:58.558
"You never watch my show?"
And I go like this, "No."

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.559
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:01.827
-That's very nice
that you have a friendship

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:02.895
that could be that honest.

00:01:02.895 --> 00:01:04.197
-He never watched me
after he left.

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:06.165
-Did you not think
you were acting it sexy?

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:07.800
-No.
-Really?

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.570
Then you have a lot of
inadvertent sexiness,

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.238
I'm sorry to tell you.
-Oh.

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:13.806
-Oh.
-What?

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:15.208
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.644
-Speaking of --
-Don't hate me 'cause I'm sexy.

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.811
-I want to congratulate you.

00:01:18.811 --> 00:01:20.547
Christopher, you've been
recently anointed ---

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:22.214
I hope that's the right term --
a zaddy.

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:24.083
Am I saying that right?
-Yes.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.319
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you, thank you.

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:30.222
And this is a council of zaddies
that gives you this honor?

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:32.859
-A coterie.
-A coterie?

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:36.763
-Yes, and it's
a worldwide organization.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.198
-For those who don't
know the term, what is --

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.500
what is a zaddy,
and what are your duties?

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.435
-I think it's
an elderly gentleman

00:01:43.435 --> 00:01:45.939
who kind of exudes
a certain athleticism,

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:47.774
maybe sex appeal.
-Yeah.

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:48.908
-Yes.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.343
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:52.778
-I think this was the photo
you submitted to the coterie.

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:55.247
-Yes, yes.
-Not too shabby.

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:57.150
-Wow.
-And they insisted

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.453
that I put my hands on the plate
just for show.

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.121
-Oh, so you didn't need
your hands?

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:03.489
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.191
-What, what?

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:07.126
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:09.161
-By the way, in case
anybody was wondering --

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:10.296
-Yeah, okay.
-You okay?

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.932
-Hey, guys, what am I, then?

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.600
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.003
-I am --
I think you only wanted

00:02:18.003 --> 00:02:19.238
to show that
because you were so worried

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:20.606
a fan was gonna be waiting
outside your house,

00:02:20.606 --> 00:02:22.508
being like,
"Why wasn't my doll --

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:25.778
Why did you show only two
of the three dolls?"

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.213
-But can I tell you something?

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.349
This fan made one for me,
Mariska,

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:31.150
and then one for Olivia,
so I got two for one.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.718
-Wow.

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:35.622
Hey, I want to congratulate you,
as well, Christopher,

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.423
on your success,
because you recently posted --

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:41.127
you went to St. Stephen's School
in Virginia.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:43.763
This was a letter home.
And I just --

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:46.498
Maybe you were not destined
for success early on.

00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:49.502
We highlighted, "While
Christopher's academic record

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:51.904
has been satisfactory --"
congratulations on that --

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:56.109
"you should know that we're
very seriously concerned

00:02:56.109 --> 00:02:58.177
about the number of demerits
he has accumulated."

00:02:58.177 --> 00:02:59.845
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.814
-Does that surprise you,
Mariska, that maybe he was --

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:02.849
-No.
-Really, yeah.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:03.950
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.351
Seems like a demerit collector
to you?

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:08.087
-Well, he beats to his own drum.
-Okay, that's right.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.321
-Would you say that's fair?
-I think

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:11.423
that's a very accurate --
-Beats to his own drum.

00:03:11.423 --> 00:03:14.994
-Is it nice to have a new sort
of entry in the franchise,

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.129
where you get to both
have crossover episodes,

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:18.597
but also do a new kind of show?
-It really is.

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:19.665
it's very liberating.

00:03:19.665 --> 00:03:21.633
I appreciate
how we tell stories.

00:03:21.633 --> 00:03:24.337
you know, and
anytime I get to work with her,

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.539
I think you would agree
that it's really --

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:29.575
it really is
special and magical,

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:31.577
and it's a gift.

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:33.112
It's like,
"Oh, she's coming on?"

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.914
You know, it's very nice.
-It's really cool.

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:37.083
And I really appreciate you guys
making the time together

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.250
with us today.
It was wonderful.

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.618
-Thank you.
-And now you're

00:03:39.618 --> 00:03:41.020
leaving the dolls for me,
or are you taking them?

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.321
-Well, I feel like
you should have one.

00:03:42.321 --> 00:03:45.491
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.326
-You guys, give it up
one more time.

00:03:47.326 --> 00:03:49.862
Mariska Hargitay,
Christopher Meloni, everybody.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.298
"Law &amp; Order: SVU" airs
Thursday nights at 9:00,

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.566
followed by
"Law &amp; Order: Organized Crime,"

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.601
right here on NBC.

